WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.120
What has life been like for Tina Majorino
since she played the side ponytail-sporting

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.740
Deb in Napoleon Dynamite?

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.759
We're taking a look back at her earliest roles
and everything she's been up to in the years

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:13.370
after that indie comedy became a cult phenomenon.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:20.580
A tiny Tina Majorino first hit the scene in
1992 in the short-lived ABC sitcom Camp Wilder

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.840
part of the famous TGIF lineup which included
hits like Full House, Family Matters, and

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.640
Boy Meets World.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.839
But not every TGIF show was a hit, and there
always seemed to be one show in the lineup

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.880
that wasn't up to par with the other three.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.520
Unfortunately, Camp Wilder belonged to latter
category, and the show was cancelled after

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.000
only 19 episodes.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.700
Camp Wilder revolved around Ricky Wilder,
a 28-year-old nurse who becomes the sole guardian

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:51.140
of her two teenage siblings after their parents'
deaths, in addition to raising her own 6-year-old

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.800
daughter, Sophie -- who was played by Majorino.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.020
Their home is turned into a sort of daycare
for her siblings and their friends, which

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.980
comes to be known as "Camp Wilder."

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.320
Famous faces like Hilary Swank, Jerry O'Connell,
and Jay Mohr appeared on the show but it was

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.560
Majorino's character who got one of the most
progressive storylines of the series.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.719
Toward the end of the show’s run, the six-year
old tells her family that she wants to be

00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:21.140
a boy, reflecting progressive transgender
awareness a couple of decades before virtually

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.220
any other show.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.620
Who could forget Waterworld, one of Hollywood's
biggest flops?

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.280
Directed by Kevin Reynolds, Waterworld told
the story of an Earth after the polar ice

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.380
caps melted, flooding the planet's land surfaces
and creating… well, a water world.

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:40.940
The movie starred Kevin Costner as a sort
of evolved fish man who helps save a kidnapped

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.140
girl named Enola, played by Majorino, who
had a mysterious tattoo on her back that ends

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.800
up being a map to dry land.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:53.119
Unfortunately, the big-budget flick got middling
reviews, with Roger Ebert calling it a picture

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:58.770
he's "not unhappy to have seen, but can't
quite recommend," and it hasn't exactly gone

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:03.320
down in history as a beloved sci-fi action
film, despite its cult following.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.960
By 2004, Majorino had grown up and out of
her childhood roles, but that didn’t stop

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.830
her from going back to high school at 19 years-old
to play Deb in the oft-quoted, quirky indie

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.440
comedy Napoleon Dynamite.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.220
“Well, is anyone else here?

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.400
trying to earn money for college.”

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.200
“Your mom goes to college!”

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.100
From the beginning of the movie, it felt like
Napoleon and Deb were meant to be, but Napoleon's

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.800
ego and his eccentric family kept getting
in the way.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:33.540
Thankfully, after a bit of high school drama,
a funky election, a lonely prom, and a couple

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.620
of good deeds, Napoleon and Deb found their
way to a romantic game of tetherball.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.280
The CW's Veronica Mars was one of those teen
shows that developed an adult audience because

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.720
it was just that good.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.900
Kristen Bell starred as Veronica Mars, the
daughter of a disgraced chief of police who

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.540
took it upon herself to solve her best friend's
murder.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.560
Majorino played Cindy "Mac" Mackenzie, a computer
whiz who had always felt a little out of place

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.200
in her family.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.460
She utilized Veronica's services to help confirm
that she was in fact switched at birth and

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.360
was actually the biological daughter of one
of the wealthiest families in Neptune.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.980
Mac and Veronica's friendship was a gal pal
match made in heaven, with Mac's tech smarts

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.070
and Veronica's sleuthing skills coming in
handy while they tried to solve the series'

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.020
many mysteries.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.840
Majorino returned as Mac in the 2014 Veronica
Mars film, and rumor has it she’ll return

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.440
for Hulu’s revival of the beloved neo-noir
show.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:35.500
HBO's Big Love followed the story of a polygamist
fundamentalist Mormon family living in Utah

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.800
and all of the drama that accompanied their
lifestyle.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:44.020
Majorino played Heather Tuttle, a young, super
conservative and devout Mormon who was best

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.120
friends with Sarah Henrickson the eldest daughter
of Bill and Barb -- played by Amanda Seyfried.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.680
Heather and Sarah work at a fast food restaurant
together for a short time and Heather keeps

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.070
the fact that her father is a state trooper
to herself, considering that what her best

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.820
friend's family is doing is pretty much illegal.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:06.440
Big Love actually marks the second TV series
in which Majorino and Seyfried acted together.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.420
Though they never shared any scenes, they
both appeared in Veronica Mars.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:15.590
Seyfried played Veronica's best friend Lily
Kane, whose murder Veronica spent most of

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.080
the show’s first season trying to solve.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.920
The cast of Grey's Anatomy truly feels like
a revolving door sometimes, with Ellen Pompeo's

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.000
Meredith Grey holding everything together.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:30.419
Majorino's Heather Brooks came aboard in season
9, right after a big plane crash season finale

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.860
that killed off a number of main characters.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.900
Brooks was an overly energetic, enthusiastic,
and bubbly character who was mostly played

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.700
for laughs as a total annoyance.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.520
“Oh, cool, is that a epidural hemorrhage?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.400
Oh, sorry, I’m interrupting.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.860
You guys were having a moment or something.”

00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:52.100
The intern did have a super sweet side, as
well as a temporary romantic dalliance with

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.840
another Grey's mainstay, Dr. Alex Karev.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.140
But alas, Majorino couldn’t escape Shonda
Rhimes’ axe.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:04.830
In Grey's Anatomy's tenth season, Brooks was
electrocuted during a storm, subsequently

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.520
having to undergo brain surgery to clear a
hemorrhage.

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:12.780
She sadly didn't make it, and the other interns
and doctors realized how much of a joy she

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.020
truly was only after she was gone.

